---
title: Thai massaman curry with chicken
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, gluten-free, one-pot, braise]
cuisine: thai
time: 1 hour 20 minutes
source: Thai Massaman Curry with Chicken by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/massaman-curry
---

== Curry paste ==

Toast the @cumin seeds{1%tsp} in a small dry #skillet{} over medium-high heat, stirring, until fragrant and a shade darker. Tip them out.

Toast the @coriander seeds{1%tsp}, @whole cloves{5} and @cardamom pods{3} the same way.

Grind the toasted spices fine with the @ground cinnamon{1%tsp} and @ground nutmeg{1/8%tsp} in a #mortar and pestle{} or spice grinder.

Mix in the @red curry paste{4-5%tbsp} and @fermented shrimp paste{1-2%tsp}.

> The paste freezes well.

== Curry ==

Grease a #heavy-bottomed pot{} with a little oil over medium-high heat. Sear the @chicken thighs{2%lb} skin down in one uncrowded layer ~{3-4%minutes} until well browned, in batches. Do not let the bits on the bottom burn.

Pour off the fat. Boil @coconut milk{1/2%cup} in the pot over medium heat.

Fry the curry paste in it, stirring often, ~{4-5%minutes} until very thick and the oil separates. Loosen with a little coconut milk and lower the heat if it sticks.

Stir in the remaining @coconut milk{1 1/2%cups}, scraping the bottom. Add the @palm sugar{3%tbsp}, half the @tamarind paste{2-3%tbsp}, half the @fish sauce{2-3%tbsp} and the @?bay leaves{2}.

Return the chicken and its juices. Simmer gently on low, partly covered, ~{35%minutes}.

Add the @waxy potatoes{10.5%oz}, @onion{1/2}(cut in 1/2-inch strips) and half the @peanuts{1/4%cup}. Top up with water so the potatoes are nearly covered. Cook over medium heat ~{10-15%minutes} until a fork slides through.

Season with the rest of the fish sauce and tamarind. The tamarind should cut the richness, not make the curry sour.

Scatter over the rest of the peanuts and serve with @jasmine rice{}.
